>>
Rule 1 (input tensor must not be int8/Char to avoid implementation error)
{v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_2) ≠ 1
>>
Rule 2 (inplace only used with floating-point inputs)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 then (dtype_(v_2) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 8)
>>
Rule 3 (input tensor’s min is not greater than its max)
{v_2 : tensor} |= min(v_2) ≤ max(v_2)
>>
Rule 4 (any dimensionality allowed; if dimensions exist, each size is non-negative)
{v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_2) > 0 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 5 (disallow complex dtypes)
{v_2 : tensor} |= (dtype_(v_2) ≠ 9) ∧ (dtype_(v_2) ≠ 10)
